      "username": "Powerhound_2000",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-10-25T12:40:33.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This is one of the questions asked and seems to address what you are talking about &nbsp;</p><p>\n&gt; </p><p>W<span>hat effect does OblivAeon coming to their reality have on their powers (increase, decrease, etc.)? Could he call the power back and turn them back into their normal form? His arrival doesn't change the powers of an OblivAeon shard as once they're separate from him they're their own thing. The biggest effect had on one of them is on Writhe as he starts to get whispers of OblivAeon [presumably through his connection to the Scion Void Soul]. He's not going to \"call the power back\" since he doesn't care. Sure they're more powerful with them, but not strong enough to defeat him (and the amount of power he'd regain from doing so is almost insignificant to him as a percentage of his overall power).</span></p><p><span>\n</span></p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:36:34.147Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
